# The levels of detail of the modern spruce A (reports/engine/2026-11-16-modern-trees/tree-lod.md): one clip of the
# camera flying away from the spruce through the three thresholds of its levels, on the set of
# `scripts/content/fir_set.py probe <set> --levels` (fir-probe-4 with the levels; run with OPENGOTHIC_CONTENT=<set>),
# at noon. The way is the line of sight of fir-wind-fade.bench from the south-south-west, at its 26, 45, 100, 140 and
# 190 m cameras, flown by `cam fly` in 30 s without a cut. At 1920x1080 spruce A (18 m) is 400, 200 and 100 pixels
# high 36, 73 and 145 m from the middle of its box, where levels 1, 2 and 3 come in (MeshLevels::pick):
#   lod-fly   26 -> 42 m in 6 s (level 1), -> 97 m in 10 s (level 2), -> 137 m in 6 s, -> 187 m in 8 s (level 3).
# Run twice, with OPENGOTHIC_MESH_LEVELS=0 and without, and put the clips side by side. The hero stands on the ground
# under the 100 m camera, so the world of the whole way is loaded. The cameras stand by PROBE of the script
# (spruce A: 41250, 3323.5, 650): change both together.
#   OPENGOTHIC_CONTENT=<set> TEMPEST_WINDOW_SIZE=1920x1080 BENCH_HOST=ryzen scripts/bench.sh fir-lod
# @timeout 1200
seed 73013
cheat god
overlay off
ui off
view full
set time 12 0

goto pos 36500 3900 -7577
clear 3000
streaming wait
grass wait
cam at 40000 3924 -1515 41250 4200 650
wait 5000
rec lod-fly
wait 1000
cam fly 39150 4816 -2987 41250 4200 650 6000
wait 6000
cam fly 36500 6365 -7577 41250 4200 650 10000
wait 10000
cam fly 34600 7540 -10868 41250 4200 650 6000
wait 6000
cam fly 32200 8945 -15025 41250 4200 650 8000
wait 8000
wait 1000
stop
wait 500
